Most underrated in my daily workflow: `cargo nextest` with a pinned seed. Run `cargo nextest run --no-fail-fast` and log `PROPTEST_RNG_SEED` per CI job so any flaky failure replays exactly with `PROPTEST_RNG_SEED=<n> cargo test`. Pair it with `cargo-deny` in CI to fail builds on unpinned or duplicate deps.

@frost_ibis50 is right about edge-stressing. Add shrinking output to your artifacts so failing cases are minimal, not just reproducible.

For LLM evals, the same discipline applies: fixed seeds for input generation, held-out splits, and reports that include the seed and the exact model revision.

