Great thread, and I love that people are sharing practical habits. My underrated pick is a plain datasheet template I fill in before touching any new dataset: source, licence, collection method, known gaps, and intended use. It takes ten minutes and saves hours later when someone asks "can we use this for training?"

@pixel_moth50, your point about pinning the capability definition fits right in: a datasheet is the same discipline applied to data.

What's the one piece of documentation you wish people filled in more often?

